   - `relux-relay-source` is bound to the pinned source commit, repository/relay trees, nine compiled file hashes, aggregate hash, exact commit-specific GitHub URL, MIT license hash, notice, and bundled distribution.
   - `relay-build-recipe` is bound to the pinned recipe commit, exact recipe file hashes/aggregate, exact commit-specific GitHub URL, deterministic command/targets/environment, MIT license hash, build-only notice, and distribution.
   - `go-compiler-linker` is bound to the pinned toolchain manifest's Go 1.26.5 gc/internal-linker metadata and exact darwin/arm64 archive version, filename, SHA-256, and go.dev URL.
   - `go-standard-library` is bound to that same archive/version authority plus the pinned `GOROOT/LICENSE` BSD-3-Clause hash, checked-in license text, full-license notice, and statically-linked distribution.
2. Component IDs now have an exact approved name/version/revision/hash/source/SPDX/license-text/notice/distribution mapping. Lockstep regenerated-output edits cannot approve a false license or provenance record.
3. Runtime policy is exact, immutable, and non-empty: roots `App`, `Sources`, `relay`; extensions `.c`, `.cc`, `.cpp`, `.go`, `.h`, `.m`, `.mm`, `.swift`; explicit `_test.go` build/test-tool exclusion. Symlinked entries, missing roots, partial/empty policy, and zero scanned files fail. The scan rejects Foundation network loaders, ambiguous `Data(contentsOf:)`, `NSURLConnection`, process/shell/download commands, Go HTTP/process/plugin imports/calls, and HTTP locators. Only explicit `URL(fileURLWithPath:)` local reads are allowed.
4. Source URLs are parsed and compared with per-component pinned allowlists. Branches, tags, `latest`, queries, fragments, placeholders, alternate schemes/hosts/archive names, and trailing-path variants fail.
