 ### 1055 — Relay supply-chain audit closes reviewer fail-open paths (TASK-260715-vtot05)
 - REVIEW REWORK: Every fixed relay/build/compiler/standard-library component now matches an authoritative pinned Git or toolchain record across identity, revision/version, content hash, exact HTTPS source allowlist, SPDX license, checked-in license hash, notice obligation, and distribution class. Lockstep edits to generated inventory/provenance can no longer legitimize a mismatched source record.
-- RUNTIME GATE: The no-download audit scope is now an exact non-empty contract over `App/`, `Sources/`, and `relay/` plus all relevant Swift/Go/Objective-C/C/C++ source kinds. It explicitly excludes Go test tooling and permits only syntactically explicit local-file `Data(contentsOf:)` reads; Foundation network loaders, ambiguous URL reads, process/shell execution, Go HTTP/process/plugin surfaces, HTTP locators, symlinked scope entries, missing roots, and partial/disabled scan policy fail closed.
-- VERIFICATION: Sixteen focused Python tests reproduce the reviewer findings and adjacent branch/tag/latest/query/fragment/placeholder/host, license-remapping, component-cross-record, runtime-scope, and symlink bypasses. Supply-chain/asset audits, 26 asset-manifest Python tests, 4 Swift manifest tests, all relay Go packages, 35 relay-release tests, Go vet, unsigned Swift build, Black, Swift format, Actionlint, JSON parsing, privacy scan, diff check, and byte-identical double generation all exit 0.
+- RUNTIME GATE: Rework 02 makes the no-download audit classify every regular file under exact `App/`, `Sources/`, and `relay/` roots. Swift, Go, Objective-C/C/C++, `.cxx`, `.hh`, `.hpp`, and `.hxx` sources are scanned; only structural Go tests and exact reviewed non-runtime paths are excluded. Unknown/new kinds fail. The scanner rejects Foundation `String`/`Data`/`NSData` URL loaders, Objective-C URL selectors, libcurl, C-family process entry points, Swift processes/shell commands, aliased/grouped Go HTTP/process/plugin imports, HTTP locators, and symlinked entries while permitting explicit local `URL(fileURLWithPath:)` reads.
+- CLAIM BOUNDARY: The gate verifies the complete classified repository runtime surface against its enumerated forbidden mechanisms. It is not a general semantic proof for arbitrary future languages; any unclassified file must fail until policy and scanner review.
+- VERIFICATION: Seventeen focused Python tests reproduce both reviewer rounds and adjacent branch/tag/latest/query/fragment/placeholder/host, license-remapping, component-cross-record, runtime-scope, source-kind, alias/grouping/comment, symlink, and safe-local controls. Supply-chain/asset audits, 26 asset-manifest Python tests, 4 Swift manifest tests, all relay Go packages, 35 relay-release tests, Go vet, unsigned Swift build, Black, Swift format, Actionlint, JSON parsing, privacy scan, diff check, and byte-identical double generation all exit 0.
 - BOARD ANOMALY: `task-board validate` exits 0 while reporting the pre-existing `EPIC-260715-2lz67t` stored `to-dev` versus child aggregate `development` mismatch. The task contract forbids weakening validation or falsifying parent dependencies, so the anomaly remains separate from this ready-for-review handoff.
 
 ### 1035 — Relay assets bind exact source/build provenance to deferred M5 release controls (TASK-260715-vtot05)
